-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Which files this MIT licence covers
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ours, under the MIT licence above:

- All scripts and data files we wrote: everything in harness/, harness/rig/,
  harness/setup/, harness/build-inputs/PREPARE_FONT_INPUT.py, memory/rig/,
  memory/rig-r5-obscura/ and engine-image/, except the two exceptions below.
- README.md, SANITISATION.md, TESTED_HASHES.json, memory/UPSTREAM.md.
- Everything in results/ (our test output and summaries).

Exceptions:

1. memory/rig/BENCHMARK.mjs follows the Campfire client puppeteer/cdp.js from
   https://github.com/lightpanda-io/demo (commit
   a87412aebbeec8b6422337fca178fbb7e3ffc883), Copyright 2023-2024 Lightpanda
   (Selecy SAS), Apache License 2.0. BENCHMARK.mjs is distributed under the
   Apache License 2.0; see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. Changes are listed in
   memory/UPSTREAM.md.

2. memory/rig/TLS_COMPAT.py quotes a six-line code block from pywebsocket3
   4.0.2 (Copyright 2020, Google Inc., BSD 3-Clause licence) so it can replace
   that block at build time. The quoted block stays under that licence; see
   LICENSES/pywebsocket3-BSD-3-Clause.txt. The rest of the file is MIT.

Not ours, and not included:

- Kan (https://github.com/kanbn/kan, AGPL-3.0). No Kan source is in this
  repository. harness/build-inputs/SOURCE_SHA256.json lists Kan file paths and
  their SHA256 values at the tested commit; it contains no Kan code.
  results/board/captures/ are screenshots of Kan's interface with synthetic
  test data, kept as test evidence.
- The browser engines and driver (Chrome for Testing, Obscura, Moli,
  Lightpanda, agent-browser). No binary or source is included; see README.md
  for links and licences.
- web-platform-tests, the Campfire test page, the Python packages in
  memory/rig/DEPENDENCIES.lock.json and the Plus Jakarta Sans font. Only
  names, URLs and hashes appear here.
